kind: calibration
question: how long does llama-quantize take from MXFP4 source to final GGUF on a 167 GB MoE, the reference the card path is compared with?
term: seconds, wall of `llama-quantize --allow-requantize --imatrix ... --tensor-type-file ...` at 64 threads, CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES empty, first read to last byte, input and output drives as arms A and B, imatrix and rules as arm A
unit: s
predict: 1200..1750
condition: the same lease, quiet host and drive layout as arms A and B, in the same sitting; normal priority (no nice); the output is the file whose sha256 arms A and B must equal
reason: fills the reference row of the promo's mid-size speed chart and gives the exactness frame its third file; why now: the card path ships with this comparison as its headline
decide-in: use it as the chart's reference; the speed-up is C / A
decide-below: the CPU was faster than the K3.1 attempt (nice 10, contended): rebase the K3.1 row 2 prediction down and say which run is the leased one
decide-above: check the thread count and the read term (an HDD-resident input would put the read over the compute); a read-bound C is a different row, not this one
